  period: c. 2500 BCE
  introduction: A celebrated bronze figurine from the Indus Valley Civilisation, depicting a young woman standing confidently with one hand resting on her hip and the other hanging by her side.
  culturalSignificance: The figurine offers a glimpse into artistic expression, craftsmanship and everyday cultural life in the Indus Valley Civilisation. Its distinctive posture and ornaments have made it one of the civilisation's best-known artefacts.
